# ── THE MEMBER'S WORK. Never tracked, so `git pull` never conflicts. ──
# The repo ships empty starters in starters/ and website-starter/. Setup copies
# them into place once, and from then on these are the member's files alone.
# Without this split, the first update you push collides with a month of their
# work and they stop pulling - which quietly turns a living repo into a snapshot.
website/
context/
keyword-map.md
website-index.md
optimization-log.md
blog-posts-log.md
scale-map-log.md
publish-schedule.md
audit-report.md
gbp-posts-queue.md
gbp-queue/
review-requests.md
review-reply-templates.md
testimonials.json
transcript-proof-candidates.md
